hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24218","Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Imran narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn al-Arqam, from his grandfather al-Arqam: That he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him, and he said: Where are you heading? He said: I intended, O Messenger of Allah, here, and he gestured with his hand toward where Bayt al-Maqdis is. He said: What takes you out to it, is it trade? He said: I said: No, but I intended prayer in it. He said: So prayer here, and he gestured toward Makkah with his hand, is better than a thousand prayers, and he gestured with his hand toward Sham."
"24219","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Imran and Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn al-Arqam narrated to me, from their grandfather al-Arqam: That he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith."
